Allow administrators to enable or disable each attendance method.

## 4.1 Employee Face Registration

Create an employee face registration workflow.

Employee registration:

1. Employee logs into the portal.
2. Opens Face Registration.
3. System requests camera permission.
4. Show live camera preview.
5. Employee captures multiple face samples.
6. Check image quality and lighting.
7. Send samples securely to the face verification provider.
8. Generate an encrypted or provider-managed face template.
9. Link the template to the employee ID.
10. Submit registration for HR approval.
11. HR reviews and approves registration.
12. Display registration status.

Face registration statuses:
- Not Registered
- Pending Verification
- Approved
- Rejected
- Expired
- Re-registration Required

Requirements:
- Support face re-registration.
- Prevent unauthorized changes to registered identity.
- Provide a manual verification alternative.
- Record consent and registration audit history.
- Never expose biometric templates to frontend users.
- Do not store biometric templates in ordinary public image storage.

## 4.2 Selfie-Based Check-In

Create a professional mobile-responsive attendance screen.

Employee workflow:

1. Employee logs in.
2. Opens My Attendance.
3. Clicks Check In.
4. Request camera permission.
5. Open live camera.
6. Capture a fresh selfie.
7. Perform liveness verification.
8. Match face with registered employee identity.
9. Capture GPS location if enabled.
10. Verify office geofence if required.
11. Validate assigned employee shift.
12. Submit attendance request to backend.
13. Backend verifies the authentication token.
14. Backend validates verification results.
15. Backend generates the official timestamp.
16. Save attendance record in Firestore.
17. Display successful check-in confirmation.

Display:
- Employee Name
- Employee ID
- Current Date
- Current Time
- Verification Status
- GPS Status
- Office Location
- Attendance Status
- Check-In Time

## 4.3 Selfie-Based Check-Out

Implement the same verification process for employee check-out.

Workflow:
1. Employee opens attendance dashboard.
2. Clicks Check Out.
3. Camera opens.
4. Capture a fresh selfie.
5. Perform liveness detection.
6. Verify registered employee identity.
7. Capture GPS if required.
8. Verify attendance session.
9. Submit request.
10. Backend generates server timestamp.
11. Save check-out record.
12. Calculate total working time.
13. Update attendance status.

Prevent:
- Check-out without check-in.
- Duplicate check-outs.
- Duplicate check-ins.
- Replayed selfies.
- Reused attendance verification sessions.
- Client-side timestamp manipulation.
- Attendance from unauthorized accounts.

Support multiple work sessions and breaks through explicit attendance events rather than overwriting timestamps.

## 4.4 Face Verification and Liveness Detection

Integrate a dedicated biometric verification service.

Requirements:
- One-to-one face matching.
- Registered employee comparison.
- Live face capture.
- Liveness verification.
- Anti-photo spoofing.
- Anti-video replay.
- Face quality validation.
- Verification confidence score.
- Verification failure tracking.

Do not automatically approve attendance based only on face detection.

Configure:
- Verification confidence threshold.
- Maximum retry attempts.
- Verification timeout.
- Manual review threshold.
- Liveness verification requirement.

If face verification fails:
- Display clear error message.
- Allow limited retries.
- Record failed attempt.
- Offer authorized manual verification.
- Do not automatically mark attendance as present.

## 4.5 GPS-Based Attendance

Implement location-based attendance.

Admin can configure:
- Company office locations.
- Office name.
- Latitude.
- Longitude.
- Permitted attendance radius.
- Multiple office branches.
- Work-from-home locations.
- Field-work attendance policy.

Employee attendance:
- Request location permission.
- Capture coordinates.
- Calculate distance from authorized location.
- Check geofence.
- Save verification result.
- Record location accuracy.
- Reject or flag attendance outside the permitted area according to company policy.

Do not silently track employees in the background. Capture location only for authorized attendance events.

## 4.6 Fingerprint Biometric Device Integration

Create a dedicated Biometric Device Management module.

Support compatible fingerprint devices through their official SDK, API, local agent, or supported attendance export format.

Features:
- Add Biometric Device.
- Device Name.
- Device ID.
- Serial Number.
- Device Location.
- Device IP Address.
- Connection Status.
- Last Synchronization.
- Employee Device ID Mapping.
- Attendance Event Import.
- Automatic Synchronization.
- Failed Event Tracking.
- Duplicate Event Detection.
- Manual Synchronization.
- Device Activity Logs.

Attendance device workflow:

1. Employee scans fingerprint.
2. Biometric device verifies fingerprint.
3. Device produces attendance event.
4. Integration service retrieves event.
5. Map device employee ID to company employee ID.
6. Validate event.
7. Identify check-in or check-out.
8. Store event in Firestore.
9. Update employee attendance.
10. Calculate working hours.

Never assume all biometric machines use the same protocol.

Do not store raw fingerprint images or templates in the payroll application unless there is a specifically approved, secure and legally compliant biometric architecture.

## 4.7 QR Code Attendance

